# Squid dstdomain allowlist -- BOOTSTRAP phase (wide).
#
# Active only while Pi is installing OpenClaw and Hermes. Switch to the
# runtime allowlist before enabling any chat channel:
#     sudo agent-egress runtime
#
# A leading dot matches the domain AND all its subdomains. Do NOT also list a
# specific host that a dotted entry already covers -- squid treats that as a
# FATAL config error ("'x.y.com' is a subdomain of '.y.com'") and refuses to
# start, which takes the whole egress policy down with it.
#
# One entry per line.

# --- Models -----------------------------------------------------------------
apps.inside.anl.gov

# --- OS packages ------------------------------------------------------------
.ubuntu.com
.debian.org
deb.nodesource.com
pkgs.tailscale.com

# --- Node / npm -------------------------------------------------------------
.npmjs.org
pi.dev
# Hermes ships its own Node runtime and fetches it from nodejs.org.
# Dotted form covers nodejs.org and its subdomains; do not also list the bare
# host or squid refuses to start.
.nodejs.org

# --- Python / pipx ----------------------------------------------------------
pypi.org
files.pythonhosted.org

# --- Source hosts (installers, release tarballs) ----------------------------
# .github.com covers github.com and codeload.github.com;
# githubusercontent.com is a separate domain and needs its own entry.
.github.com
.githubusercontent.com

# --- Agent installers -------------------------------------------------------
.openclaw.ai
.nousresearch.com
